Kasper asked:
"And what about your job?"
I thought for a moment.
Then Sara asked about my first day at the software company.
I was quite nervous that morning.
I took the bus to work.
I looked out the window and thought about my new colleagues.
I walked into the big building.
I stood in the new office and said hello.
A man quickly came over to me.
"Welcome to Denmark, my name is Peter," he said kindly.
Peter smiled broadly and showed me my new desk.
He was my new colleague.
We drank a cup of coffee together.
He asked about my long journey from Mexico.
It was very pleasant, and I relaxed.
Sara nodded and looked at me.
"Good colleagues are incredibly important," she said.
I completely agreed.
